        "title": "Downgrade tiktoken to 1.0.15 and add token count fallback",
        "summary": "Backend downgrades `tiktoken` from 1.0.16 to 1.0.15 in `package.json`. `countTokens` in `backend/src/util/token-counter.ts` now wraps encoding in a try-catch, returning `Math.ceil(text.length / 3)` on error. Scope limited to backend utilities.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:28:10.796Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If the assistant's token counter runs into a problem calculating how many pieces a message breaks into, it now quietly falls back to a quick estimate instead of breaking. The backend uses an older, more stable version of its counting library to keep things steady while still letting your request go through normally.",
