        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "backend deploy.sh parameterizes image name and adds timestamp tag",
        "summary": "backend/deploy.sh replaces hardcoded manicode-backend image references with $VM_NAME variable and generates a timestamped Docker tag. Adds backend/.dockerignore to exclude node_modules and debug files from build context. Updates todo.knowledge.md with new bug reports regarding terminal control and reconnection states.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:28:15.412Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the team deploys new backend code, the script now labels each uploaded image with the machine's name and a timestamp instead of always calling it the same default name. This means you only build and reuse images that actually belong to this specific environment, so a test setup can't accidentally grab production code. Behind the scenes, the build process also skips copying debug logs and dependency files, keeping uploads smaller and avoiding stale debug data leaking between versions. The engineers also noted two new bugs they're tracking: the terminal sometimes won't release control after running commands, and reconnection attempts may report success without actually resuming work.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
